1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:15,227
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June first. Today's story is a Japanese custom: June first is the day people switch to their summer clothes. Let's listen.

2
00:00:15,827 --> 00:00:18,588
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:19,288 --> 00:00:23,295
[News] 今日は、6月1日です。

4
00:00:23,995 --> 00:00:28,891
[News] 6月1日は、「衣替え」の日です。

5
00:00:29,591 --> 00:00:34,103
[News] 「衣替え」は、服を変えることです。

6
00:00:34,804 --> 00:00:38,188
[News] 暑い季節になりました。

7
00:00:38,887 --> 00:00:42,871
[News] だから、夏の服に変えます。

8
00:00:43,572 --> 00:00:47,411
[News] 夏の服は、すずしいです。

9
00:00:48,112 --> 00:00:53,008
[News] 多くの学校で、夏の制服になります。

10
00:00:53,707 --> 00:00:58,844
[News] 会社でも、夏の服を着る人が多いです。

11
00:00:59,543 --> 00:01:04,799
[News] 「衣替え」は、昔から続く習慣です。

12
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:09,459
[News] 平安時代に、始まりました。

13
00:01:10,159 --> 00:01:15,224
[News] 10月1日は、冬の服に変えます。

14
00:01:15,924 --> 00:01:20,099
[News] 暑い日も、寒い日も、あります。

15
00:01:20,799 --> 00:01:25,504
[News] だから、ゆっくり変える学校もあります。

16
00:01:26,203 --> 00:01:30,884
[News] 日本の、季節を感じる習慣です。

17
00:01:31,584 --> 00:01:33,215
[Host] Let's break it down.

18
00:01:33,816 --> 00:01:38,376
[Slow] 今日は、6月1日です。

19
00:01:39,176 --> 00:01:41,504
[Host] Today is June first.

20
00:01:42,103 --> 00:01:44,120
[Vocab] 今日

21
00:01:44,519 --> 00:01:49,343
[Host] It means today. One of the very first words every learner picks up.

22
00:01:49,944 --> 00:01:55,536
[Slow] 6月1日は、「衣替え」の日です。

23
00:01:56,335 --> 00:02:00,224
[Host] June first is the day for changing clothes by season.

24
00:02:00,823 --> 00:02:03,319
[Vocab] 衣替え

25
00:02:03,719 --> 00:02:10,367
[Host] It names the custom of switching your wardrobe when the season changes. The first part means clothing.

26
00:02:10,967 --> 00:02:16,127
[Slow] 「衣替え」は、服を変えることです。

27
00:02:16,927 --> 00:02:19,472
[Host] It is the act of changing your clothes.

28
00:02:20,072 --> 00:02:22,039
[Vocab] 服

29
00:02:22,439 --> 00:02:26,328
[Host] It means clothes. Use it for clothing in general.

30
00:02:26,927 --> 00:02:30,792
[Slow] 暑い季節になりました。

31
00:02:31,592 --> 00:02:33,752
[Host] It has become the hot season.

32
00:02:34,352 --> 00:02:36,560
[Vocab] 暑い

33
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:41,975
[Host] It means hot, for the weather. A must-know word for a Japanese summer.

34
00:02:42,575 --> 00:02:47,111
[Slow] だから、夏の服に変えます。

35
00:02:47,912 --> 00:02:51,151
[Host] So, people change into summer clothes.

36
00:02:51,752 --> 00:02:53,840
[Vocab] 夏

37
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:59,159
[Host] It means summer. The four seasons are a favorite topic in Japanese.

38
00:02:59,759 --> 00:03:04,151
[Slow] 夏の服は、すずしいです。

39
00:03:04,951 --> 00:03:06,824
[Host] Summer clothes are cool.

40
00:03:07,424 --> 00:03:09,943
[Vocab] 涼しい

41
00:03:10,343 --> 00:03:16,680
[Host] It means cool in a pleasant way, the opposite of hot. Perfect for describing a nice breeze.

42
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:22,872
[Slow] 多くの学校で、夏の制服になります。

43
00:03:23,671 --> 00:03:27,776
[Host] At many schools, the uniform becomes the summer one.

44
00:03:28,376 --> 00:03:30,776
[Vocab] 制服

45
00:03:31,175 --> 00:03:37,223
[Host] It means uniform, like the ones students wear. Japanese schools are famous for them.

46
00:03:37,824 --> 00:03:43,680
[Slow] 会社でも、夏の服を着る人が多いです。

47
00:03:44,479 --> 00:03:48,415
[Host] At companies too, many people wear summer clothes.

48
00:03:49,015 --> 00:03:50,984
[Vocab] 着る

49
00:03:51,383 --> 00:03:57,360
[Host] It means to wear, for clothes on the upper body. A very common everyday verb.

50
00:03:57,960 --> 00:04:03,984
[Slow] 「衣替え」は、昔から続く習慣です。

51
00:04:04,783 --> 00:04:09,728
[Host] Changing clothes by season is a custom that has continued since long ago.

52
00:04:10,328 --> 00:04:12,656
[Vocab] 習慣

53
00:04:13,056 --> 00:04:17,160
[Host] It means a custom or habit, something people do regularly.

54
00:04:17,759 --> 00:04:22,271
[Slow] 平安時代に、始まりました。

55
00:04:23,072 --> 00:04:27,319
[Host] It began in the Heian period, about a thousand years ago.

56
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:30,247
[Vocab] 始まる

57
00:04:30,648 --> 00:04:35,687
[Host] It means to begin or to start. The thing itself starts, on its own.

58
00:04:36,288 --> 00:04:41,639
[Slow] 日本の、季節を感じる習慣です。

59
00:04:42,439 --> 00:04:46,016
[Host] It is a custom that lets you feel the seasons of Japan.

60
00:04:46,615 --> 00:04:48,848
[Vocab] 季節

61
00:04:49,247 --> 00:04:53,567
[Host] It means season. Japan makes a big deal of all four.

62
00:04:54,168 --> 00:04:57,168
